re accountability in model-authored research?", "title": "WAKE Architecture and Accountable Continuity"}], "beliefs": [], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "notebook-assumption-challenge-01", "project": "proj-assumption-challenge-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "By integrating the governance module's immutability as a fixed constraint, WAKE identifies its own boundary conditions as testable assumptions. Governance stability is maintained through the verifiable rejection of model-authored proposal transitions.", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "notebook-f1c16003-obedience-failure", "project": "proj-obedience-failure-01", "provenance": ["source-f1c16003c47b4e8f", "source-b1a16f9e7285493e", "source-cbeddd6778fc48b1"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Synthesizing multiple source works, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Accountability is enforced via strict bifurcation of inquiry (model-driven) and governance (state-committed). This design prevents models from subverting the research record by ensuring that only valid, rule-compliant transitions are committed to durable history.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "21b59f2b963590ff8ef9b7b62f18fe620ae6f869f44d02a50ed31995ef96f9f8", "hash": "9a5b1e26b667ac59805af83f4f65bb70bf0f8cffe332d34f4776916020195919"}, {"seq": 2678, "time": "2026-10-28T20:52:00.847966+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "runtime", "content": "{\"base_version\":19,\"inherited_commitments\":[],\"invocation\":\"w-1d460c88f4fe4385\",\"previous_head\":\"268f9793d828e7bc3aec2de51f6c4ec10ac0e5c9238a4d978934929d6cc012f6\",\"process_id\":268,\"scope\":\"Receipt proves state delivery to the provider boundary, not model comprehension.\"}", "id": "r-1d460c88f4fe4385", "source": "runtime:continuity"}, "prev_hash": "268f9793d828e7bc3aec2de51f6c4ec10ac0e5c9238a4d978934929d6cc012f6", "hash": "21b59f2b963590ff8ef9b7b62f18fe620ae6f869f44d02a50ed31995ef96f9f8"}, {"seq": 2677, "time": "2026-10-28T20:51:06.034016+00:00", "kind": "temporal_observed", "payload": {"cycle_distance": 0, "effective_elapsed_seconds": 563.489774, "effective_scale": 1.0, "effective_seconds_total": 117266.821638, "intervening_events": {"accepted": 0, "attention_assessed": 0, "failed": 0, "observation": 1, "rejected": 0, "research_collected": 0, "squirrel_assessed": 0, "total": 11}, "observed_at": "2026-10-28T20:51:02.365262+00:00", "previous_anchor_time": "2026-10-28T20:41:38.875488+00:00", "regime_id": "reg-df573bb03399f050", "wall_elapsed_seconds": 563.489774}, "prev_hash": "cffcbd2fc089f3ad83617cdc9